# Follow Me — local configuration. `cp .env.example .env`, then fill in section 1.
#
# Three sections, in the order you need them:
#   1. Required to boot — the app shows a setup screen until all five are set
#   2. Optional         — unset is fine; the named feature degrades, nothing breaks
#   3. Not the app      — Edge Function secrets and integration-test inputs
#
# The fastest way through section 1 is `supabase start`, which gives you a local
# database and a local classify-photos endpoint with no accounts at all — see
# README → "Getting started" → "Option A: everything local".
#
# Section 2 is left commented out on purpose: an unset key degrades cleanly, a
# key set to a placeholder does not.
#
# All EXPO_PUBLIC_* values are inlined into the JS bundle at build time. That
# makes them public by design (RLS is the security boundary, not secrecy), and
# it means changing one needs `npx expo start -c` — a plain reload keeps the old
# value. Never put a service-role key or an API secret behind this prefix.


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1. REQUIRED TO BOOT — the list enforced in src/infrastructure/env.ts
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Supabase — database, auth and Edge Functions.
# Local:  `supabase start` prints both values (API URL + anon key).
# Cloud:  Dashboard → Project Settings → Data API (URL) and API Keys (anon).
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your_supabase_anon_key_here

# Cloudinary — where photos are uploaded before they go out to followers.
# Free tier is plenty. Cloud name: Dashboard, top left. Upload preset: Settings
# → Upload → Add upload preset, with Signing Mode set to **Unsigned** — the app
# uploads straight from the device, with no server-side signature.
EXPO_PUBLIC_CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME=your_cloud_name
EXPO_PUBLIC_CLOUDINARY_UPLOAD_PRESET=your_unsigned_upload_preset

# AI photo classification — the `classify-photos` Edge Function's endpoint.
# Local:  http://127.0.0.1:54321/functions/v1/classify-photos (supabase functions serve)
# Cloud:  Dashboard → Edge Functions → classify-photos → copy the endpoint URL.
# The URL being public is fine: the function REQUIRES a signed-in user's JWT
# (the bare anon key is rejected) and enforces a per-user daily quota.
EXPO_PUBLIC_CLASSIFY_FN_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321/functions/v1/classify-photos


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 2. OPTIONAL — leave unset locally; each degrades on its own
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Cloudinary folder. Unset → uploads land in the root, which is what production
# does. Staging builds set "staging" so test uploads never mix with real assets.
# Degrades to: no folder param on the upload.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_CLOUDINARY_FOLDER=staging

# MapTiler — satellite imagery for the Me-page travel globe (issue #78).
# Sign up at maptiler.com and copy a key.
# Degrades to: MapLibre's free demo tiles, a plain vector world with no imagery
# (src/ui/map/styleUrl.ts), and a place picker that offers no suggestions
# (MapTilerPlaceSearch returns nothing on an empty key). Both are keyless.
# The key ships inside the app like any other EXPO_PUBLIC_ value, so protect it
# with the allowed-origins/referrer restrictions in the MapTiler dashboard
# rather than by keeping it secret. The real value ships via eas.json build env.
#
# Tiles only. Geocoding stays off MapTiler entirely — it bills per request and
# every map tile already spends from the same quota, while BigDataCloud (the
# in-app reverse lookup that names a posting's place) is keyless and free.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_MAPTILER_KEY=your_maptiler_key

# Sentry — crash & error monitoring (issue #10). The DSN is safe to expose (it
# only lets clients SEND events); get it from sentry.io → Project Settings →
# Client Keys. Degrades to: no reporting at all — which is what you want
# locally, since monitoring only activates in EAS preview/production builds
# anyway (EXPO_PUBLIC_APP_VARIANT gates it). Ships via eas.json, not this file.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=https://your-key@o0.ingest.sentry.io/0
# Source-map upload (CI / EAS build only — never needed locally):
# SENTRY_ORG, SENTRY_PROJECT as EAS env vars + GitHub Actions vars, and
# SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN as an EAS secret + GitHub Actions secret.


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 3. NOT READ BY THE APP — server-side secrets and test inputs
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Nothing here affects whether the app boots. Skip the section entirely unless
# you are working on an Edge Function or running the integration suites.

# Edge Function secrets. In the cloud these are set per project with
# `supabase secrets set --project-ref <ref> KEY=value`, never from this file.
# Locally, `supabase functions serve --env-file .env` reads them from here.
#   GEMINI_API_KEY        — aistudio.google.com; the only one classify-photos needs
#   GEMINI_MODEL          — optional model override
#   CLASSIFY_DAILY_QUOTA  — optional per-user daily cap override
#   CLOUDINARY_API_KEY / _API_SECRET / _CLOUD_NAME — asset cleanup in delete-candidates
#   CRON_SECRET           — the x-cron-secret header auto-post requires
#   GALLERY_BASE_URL      — public gallery links in outgoing messages
#   TWILIO_STATUS_CALLBACK_URL / TWILIO_WEBHOOK_URL — Twilio callbacks
# SUPABASE_URL and SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY are injected by the platform.

# Twilio — WhatsApp delivery. Server-side only: the app never holds these, it
# calls the send-post function. Needed to actually deliver a post to a follower;
# everything up to the send works without them.
TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=ACxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=your_auth_token_here
TWILIO_WHATSAPP_FROM=+14155238886

# Integration tests only (`npm run test:integration`). Every suite skips itself
# when its variables are unset, so `npm test` never needs any of them.
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY       — repository suites (Dashboard → API Keys)
#   AUTH_TEST_PHONE / AUTH_TEST_OTP — Supabase test phone number + its fixed OTP
#   CLASSIFY_FN_URL / CLASSIFY_FN_KEY — classify-photos suite
#   AUTO_POST_FN_URL + CRON_SECRET  — auto-post suite
#   WHATSAPP_TEST_RECIPIENT         — real number the WhatsApp suite messages
WHATSAPP_TEST_RECIPIENT=+1234567890
